  "claim": "At commit 8904bf09 of https://github.com/kbr-/math-research, the Lean declaration MathResearch.bitPHP_exponential states that for every l >= 32 every refutation of the usual bit pigeonhole clause set with 2^l+1 pigeons has more than exp(2^l/(32768 l^2)) lines, in a proof system of linear clauses over F2 whose rules include complementary-parity resolution on any affine form, semantic weakening and every sound inference from at most two earlier lines, with unrestricted reuse and size equal to the number of lines. Every standard rule set of DAG-like Res(\u2295) is contained in it, so the formal theorem implies the bound for standard Res(\u2295). The formal clause set is unsatisfiable for every l and the formal system refutes the instance l = 1, so the statement is not vacuous.",
